# T-0323: tickets.md is a shared, append-mostly ledger -- concurrent
# worktrees appending near the same line otherwise produce a false
# textual conflict (T-0176's class). Route it through the frob-ledger
# merge driver (splice_ledger, id-level/state-rank/evidence-union
# resolution) instead of git's default line-level merge.
#
# The driver itself must still be registered locally (a .gitattributes
# entry alone does not install it, by git's own design -- see
# docs/modules/tickets.md#git-merge-driver for the one-time
# `git config merge.frob-ledger.*` setup):
#
#   git config merge.frob-ledger.name "frob ticket ledger splice"
#   git config merge.frob-ledger.driver "frob ticket merge-driver %O %A %B"
#
# T-0480: the pattern MUST be anchored with a leading slash so it matches
# ONLY the root ledger. An unanchored `tickets.md` also matches
# `docs/modules/tickets.md` (and any other file so named), and the ledger
# driver then truncates that documentation to a bare 3-line ledger header
# with NO conflict markers -- silent ~900-line doc loss during any merge.
/tickets.md merge=frob-ledger
/tickets-archive.md merge=frob-ledger

# T-1258: ledger v2 (docs/design/ledger-v2.md section 5) retires this
# driver's NEED once a repo is v2-only -- disjoint `tickets/T-####/`
# directories are ordinary git objects git's native per-file 3-way merge
# already resolves correctly, with zero conflict for two branches editing
# different tickets and an ordinary (non-spliced) conflict for two
# branches editing the SAME ticket. This repo itself still stores tickets
# in the v1 monofile (`tickets.md`/`tickets-archive.md` above), so the two
# lines above stay in force; removing them is the migration ticket's
# final-cutover step (design section 7.4), not this ticket's -- see
# docs/design/ledger-v2.md#7-reversible-migration-plan-design-for-the-child-ticket-not-built-here.
